    <string name="gapps_switch_detail">For experienced users: puts the apps of a package you supply into the new system. It is not certified by Google, and some apps won\'t work. You pick the file on the next page.</string>
    <string name="gapps_overline">ADVANCED</string>
    <string name="gapps_title">Add a Google apps package</string>
    <string name="gapps_lede">OpenBook can put a Google apps package you supply into the new system. OpenBook never downloads one, and doesn\'t say where to get one.</string>
    <string name="gapps_requirements">You need a package for Android 17 (SDK 37) on x86_64, in LiteGapps\' layout: a .zip file with module.prop and files/files.tar.br or files/files.tar.xz. Put it on this stick\'s storage (Downloads, for example) or on a USB drive. Only apps and their permission settings are accepted: anything that would change the system itself is refused.</string>
